<?php
/**
 * Spartrak — the global loader, pre-rendered for NAVIGATION.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * IT IS MAGENTO'S OWN OVERLAY SHAPE, ON PURPOSE
 * ===========================================================================
 * `.loading-mask > .loader` is exactly what lib/web/mage/loader.js builds, and
 * therefore exactly what components/_loader.less already draws the Spartrak
 * ring inside — the scrim and the fixed positioning come from core's
 * _loaders.less, the ring from this theme's `.loader::before`. So this adds no
 * styling, no second spinner and no second visual language. It is the project
 * loader (CLAUDE.md section 10), raised by a trigger Magento does not have one
 * for: a full page reload.
 *
 * WHY IT IS PRE-RENDERED RATHER THAN BUILT BY THE WIDGET, and why the class
 * on <html> is what shows it, is in js/spartrak-nav-pending.js — the short
 * version is that the widget's template contains `<img src="">`, which a
 * browser resolves to a second request for the current page.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHAT IS AND IS NOT IN THE MARKUP
 * ===========================================================================
 * NO <img>. The widget emits one and components/_loader.less hides it; a
 * hidden image is still fetched, and that residual is recorded at the top of
 * that file. Since this instance is authored rather than generated, the honest
 * thing is simply not to emit it — the ring is a CSS pseudo-element and needs
 * no asset.
 *
 * THE <p> STAYS, and it is the reason this template exists at all rather than
 * a bare div. It is the only thing that tells a screen-reader user the page is
 * busy. `role="status"` — which core's own loader markup does NOT carry — makes
 * it a polite live region, so revealing it announces; without that it would be
 * text nobody hears (CLAUDE.md section 15). It is visually hidden by
 * components/_loader.less's `.loader > p` rule, the same as everywhere else.
 *
 * `aria-hidden` is deliberately absent: the overlay is inert while
 * `display: none` and must be announceable the moment it is not.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * COST
 * ===========================================================================
 * ~180 bytes of markup and one ~1.5KB module, mounted only on the routes that
 * need it (see the layout files that include this block) rather than
 * site-wide. No request, no image, no widget. The overlay is `display: none`
 * until the class lands, so it costs nothing to paint and cannot affect LCP.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */
?>
<div class="loading-mask spartrak-nav-loader" data-role="loader">
    <div class="loader">
        <p role="status"><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Please wait...')) ?></p>
    </div>
</div>
<script type="text/x-magento-init">
    {
        "*": {
            "spartrakNavPending": {}
        }
    }
</script>
